       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day. That is well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 2,000 mg dose is also double the usual 1,000 mg maximum. At this level there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function and a 70 kg weight.\n\nHere are some options that fit the dosing limits:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the 2000 mg dose was a typo, for example if you meant 1000 mg or 200 mg, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it. If you really do want the dose as written, for a reason I don't know about, tell me and add the clinical rationale. I'd still want it reviewed by pharmacy before I enter it."
      }
